# App workflow (locked)

Full doc: `docs/APP_WORKFLOW.md` · route table: `example/router/routes.ts`

## example vs docs (locked)

| | **example** | **docs** |
|--|----------|----------|
| Role | **Local debug tool** for library authors | **Public VitePress site** for app developers |
| Deploy | **Never** ship/deploy online | **Yes** — pack and host |
| Content | Half-done pages, stress tests, verbose logs, bug repro, perf / edge triage | Clean standard examples, API params, tutorials only |
| Forbid | Using example as the public demo | Putting stress / bug-repro pages in docs |

## Directories
- **Library** → `packages/` (no routes, no mock pages).
- **Debug shell** → `example/` local-only: `layouts/` · `pages/` · `router/` · `stores/` · `mock/`.
- **Official docs** → `docs/` (VitePress): API + guides + standard demos.
- Pages only in `example/pages/**/**Page.vue`. Business UI in `packages/components/business/<domain>`; pages stay thin.

## Seven debug zones (`meta.group`) — example only
`overview` · `intro` · `base` · `biz` · `theme` · `i18n` · `perf` · `lab` · `dev`
(`perf` / `dev/bug-repro` stay in example — never promote to docs.)

## Routes
- Single table `example/router/routes.ts`; navigate by `name` only.
- Auth gate: `meta.public`. Shell: `meta.requiresAuth` + `group` + `title` + `icon`.
- Theme `?design=linear`; locale `?lang=ja-JP` at boot.

## Start
```
npm run dev        # example — local only
npm run docs:dev   # official docs authoring
npm run build      # lib → dist/ (publish)
npm run build:example # optional local smoke → example-dist/ (DO NOT deploy)
```
Node ≥ 18. Boot: Font → IconStyle → Theme → URL → app + router.

## Demo layout (locked)
`DemoBlock` · `DemoCode` · curated demos span the full `.ln-content` column.
See `vue3-amg-webui-example-demo-layout.mdc` — no prose `max-width` on demo chrome; no nested `max-height` on code panels.

## Don’t
- Deploy example / `example-dist` as the public demo or docs substitute.
- String `currentPage` navigation; `*Page.vue` under `packages/`.
- Put stress tests or bug-repro flows into the VitePress docs site.
- Shrink-wrap component docs / code samples with reading-column `max-width` or capped code panels.
